---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { livePosts } from '../lib/posts';
import { formatDate, site } from '../lib/site';

// MIMIC: home copy below is a first pass written by Dash for Mimic to rewrite/unslop. Keep facts general; no invented numbers.
const posts = await livePosts();
const description = 'Practical, sourced guides for owning a Japanese import car in New Zealand: batteries, running costs, WoF, rust and buying checks.';
---

<Base title={site.name} description={description} path="/" pageTitle={`${site.name}: ${site.tagline}`}>
	<section class="hero">
		<h1>{site.name}</h1>
		<p class="tagline">{site.tagline}</p>
		<p>
			A Japanese import is cheap to buy and easy to love, and then the questions start. Is that Leaf battery healthy? What does a hybrid pack cost to
			replace? Will it pass a WoF? What will it really cost to run each week?
		</p>
		<p>
			This site answers one question per guide, with the answer first, the sources listed and a date showing when each fact was last checked.
			We lean on NZTA and other primary sources, we say when we are unsure, and we never guess at numbers.
		</p>
		<div class="answer-box">
			<strong>How to use it.</strong> Start with the buying and battery guides if you are shopping. Start with running costs and servicing if you already own one.
			Every guide links to the bigger guide it belongs to and to related posts.
		</div>
	</section>
	<h2>Latest guides</h2>
	{
		posts.length === 0 ? (
			<p>The first guides are being finished and will appear here one a day.</p>
		) : (
			<ol class="archive">
				{posts.map((post) => (
					<li>
						<a href={`/posts/${post.id}`}>
							<h3>{post.data.title}</h3>
							<p class="dek">{post.data.description}</p>
							<time datetime={post.data.pubDate.toISOString()}>{formatDate(post.data.pubDate)}</time>
						</a>
					</li>
				))}
			</ol>
		)
	}
</Base>
